WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:06.000
Today I want to talk about something that is absolutely king when it comes to trading, and that is market structure.

00:06.600 --> 00:12.760
If you can understand market structure, then you can identify those areas where the price is likely to get a really big move.

00:13.240 --> 00:19.140
And market structure is king. It determines which way the trend is going, it determines which way the price is likely to go in the future,

00:19.660 --> 00:25.780
and it gives you points in which you can identify what is objectively high, what is objectively low,

00:25.780 --> 00:30.960
and if the price is getting a pullback, where you can then look for support to look for a long,

00:31.060 --> 00:33.840
or if we're getting a pullback to the upside, you can look for resistance to short.

00:34.280 --> 00:40.000
And if you understand market structure, you know where to put your stop losses so that your trading idea gets invalidated at the right place.

00:40.140 --> 00:44.440
You know where to put your take profits so that you're making the proper risk-to-reward ratio setups.

00:44.820 --> 00:48.080
And it pretty much dictates everything when it comes to the way the markets move.

00:48.240 --> 00:53.680
And so today, we're going to be diving deep into market structure, a very simple concept.

00:53.680 --> 00:58.040
But a lot of people mess this up, so make sure to stick around until the end of the video.

00:58.580 --> 01:02.000
You don't want to miss this one, and make sure to go back and watch the first parts of this series

01:02.000 --> 01:05.080
if you really want an in-depth day trading guide.

01:05.200 --> 01:07.140
All right, so first of all, what is market structure?

01:07.240 --> 01:12.480
A very simple concept. A lot of people like to overcomplicate this to make themselves seem smarter than they really are.

01:12.920 --> 01:18.100
Basically, market structure is a way to determine whether you are in an uptrend or a downtrend.

01:18.480 --> 01:21.800
So we're going to come over here to a blank chart with no markings on it,

01:21.800 --> 01:25.940
and we're just going to identify whether or not price is in an uptrend or a downtrend.

01:26.060 --> 01:31.000
The way you can tell that price is an uptrend is because the price makes higher lows and higher highs.

01:31.280 --> 01:34.400
If you see right here, we make this low, and then we make a high.

01:34.920 --> 01:39.840
If it's now made a higher high than the last swing high, well, guess what?

01:39.960 --> 01:42.720
Now we've officially switched into bullish market structure,

01:42.920 --> 01:48.740
and we would expect a higher low to come in, and then eventually a higher high to come in.

01:48.740 --> 01:51.260
And that's exactly what we see happening right now.

01:51.580 --> 01:55.580
This is how you can determine whether or not you are in an uptrend or a downtrend.

01:55.700 --> 02:00.660
If we zoom out and we go back a little bit farther, you can see that price was in a local downtrend.

02:00.780 --> 02:06.520
Why? Well, because we made a high, and then we made a low, and then we made our first lower high,

02:06.800 --> 02:09.960
and so we would expect that we would make a lower low, which we did.

02:10.040 --> 02:11.820
Then we would expect we'd make a lower high, which we did.

02:12.060 --> 02:13.800
Then we expect we'd make a lower low, which we did.

02:13.800 --> 02:16.840
And we would expect to make a lower high, which we did.

02:17.480 --> 02:19.060
Now here's where things change.

02:19.540 --> 02:23.200
Instead of then making a lower low, what do we do?

02:23.280 --> 02:26.820
We make a higher low, and then we make our higher high.

02:27.440 --> 02:31.600
And so once you change the pattern of higher lows and higher highs,

02:31.840 --> 02:37.020
you have officially switched market structure from bearish into bullish.

02:37.020 --> 02:44.200
All right, just to draw an uptrend, bullish market structure is up a lot, down a little.

02:44.660 --> 02:45.980
Up a lot, down a little.

02:46.360 --> 02:47.840
Up a lot, down a little.

02:48.100 --> 02:54.540
As soon as you take out this last low, we have switched now into bearish market structure.

02:55.100 --> 03:00.840
You don't know necessarily if this is a lower high, although in hindsight, you can tell that this was a lower high.

03:00.840 --> 03:06.320
But until we actually make a lower low, you can't assume that we're going to make a lower high.

03:06.920 --> 03:10.560
So once you change that structure, we're making higher highs and higher lows.

03:10.680 --> 03:14.340
As soon as you cross that line where you've officially made a lower low,

03:14.680 --> 03:19.840
now you look for an actual lower high to change into bearish market structure.

03:19.840 --> 03:25.040
When we go to Bitcoin on the high timeframes, like the monthly,

03:25.460 --> 03:30.900
I just want to show you that when we changed market structure right here,

03:31.220 --> 03:35.040
and we put in a lower low on the monthly, which we confirmed in February's candle,

03:35.500 --> 03:40.900
